    "result_text": "All 283 tests pass with **BUILD SUCCESS**, including the new `Cp17Tests`. (The single `GeneralExceptionHandler` error log line is an intentional error-path assertion in an unrelated controller test that passes.)\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `sharesHousehold` flag for owner creation on `POST /api/owners`, following the existing OfficeFloor function-injection pattern.\n\n**What \"shares household\" means:** at creation time, `true` if another owner already has the same address and city (compared case- and whitespace-insensitively), else `false`. Creation always proceeds regardless.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`Owner` model** \u2014 added a `Boolean sharesHousehold` field (`@Column(name = \"shares_household\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n2. **Schemas** \u2014 added a `shares_household BOOLEAN` column to all four DDL files (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres). Tests run on hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column had to be declared explicitly.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `sharesHousehold` boolean property to the `Owner` schema, which regenerates `OwnerDto` with the field. MapStruct maps it by name automatically, so both `POST` (create) and `GET` responses carry it.\n\n4. **New step `ComputeSharesHousehold`** \u2014 a function class that scans existing owners (excluding the one being created) for a matching normalized address + city, mirroring the normalization used in `NormalizeCity`/`EnsureOwnerUnique`.\n\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new `computeSharesHousehold` step into the pipeline after `assignCustomerCode` and before `save` (under the `transaction` governance), so the flag is computed against the pre-save owner set and persisted.\n\nThe test's flow (POST then GET the flag back) works because the value is persisted on the entity and surfaced through the DTO on both endpoints.",
